d/1398021-dark-souls-3-s-paired-greatswords-aka-the-most-dawn-weapon-ever#post1398021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would absolutely give my next character who's a melee fighter weapons like these except the rules actually make something like this impossible without evocations as you can't actually dual-wield grand daiklaves, lol</div> </div> </div> </div> You actually can, using a Merit from <i>the Realm</i> (which requires the Giant Merit).<br /> <br /> Of course, because two-handed weapons and paired weapons provide the exact same bonus, there no reason to do it beyond aesthetics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T11:33:50-07:00","id":1398027,"title":"","content":"I too am fond of Dark Souls III as an example of some particularly fancy looking large weapons that are swung about with speed and dexterity, with some interesting lore to boot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398021-dark-souls-3-s-paired-greatswords-aka-the-most-dawn-weapon-ever?p=1398024#post1398024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course, because two-handed weapons and paired weapons provide the exact same bonus, there no reason to do it beyond aesthetics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if they're two <i>different</i> grand daiklaves...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T12:02:03-07:00","id":1398034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398021-dark-souls-3-s-paired-greatswords-aka-the-most-dawn-weapon-ever#post1398021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would absolutely give my next character who's a melee fighter weapons like these except the rules actually make something like this impossible without evocations as you can't actually dual-wield grand daiklaves, lol</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see part of the attunement bonus granting you the power to dual wield the swords, especially as, as other have mentioned, wielding two grand daiklaves isn't actually mechanically better than two-handing a single one. Aside from making it harder to completely disarm you.<br /> <br /> Either the rest of the attunement bonus, or actual Evocations alone, would need to introduce more mechanical benefits for using a pair of grand daiklaves.<br /> <br /> All of which would probably be counterbalanced by losing those benefits if someone disarms you of one sword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-21-2020, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T12:04:52-07:00","id":1398035,"title":"","content":"Eska of the Seven Blades has short daiklaves that as a passive ability give her an additional +2 to clash attacks if she's wielding all 6 at once.<br /> So that could be your basis for being strong enough to dual wield two-handed weapons.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T15:25:23-07:00","id":1398074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398021-dark-souls-3-s-paired-greatswords-aka-the-most-dawn-weapon-ever?p=1398027#post1398027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I too am fond of Dark Souls III as an example of some particularly fancy looking large weapons that are swung about with speed and dexterity, with some interesting lore to boot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. It's hard to translate a lot of lore of Souls into Exalted, as Souls is extremely pessimistic and nihilist, whereas Exalted is less so, but it does provide a lot of great stuff to use for darker games if you translate it properly.<br /> <br /> Also, one day I want to turn the Pyromancy and Miracle spells into martial arts each because chucking massive lightning spears is absolutely something a Solar should be able to do.<br /> <br /> (DS3 could also be good inspiration for a worst-timeline game where everything goes to absolute hell to the point of reality itself breaking down, and Gael's mission to create a new world with the painting could inspire a jaded pessimistic Solar or Infernal with a similar mission of just restarting everything through some unfathomably powerful artifact)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4801,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","user":"Frostav","date":". 06-21-2020, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T17:20:54-07:00","id":1398089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1398021-dark-souls-3-s-paired-greatswords-aka-the-most-dawn-weapon-ever?p=1398074#post1398074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup. It's hard to translate a lot of lore of Souls into Exalted, as Souls is extremely pessimistic and nihilist, whereas Exalted is less so</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though Artifacts provide fertile ground in general to be their own self-contained cosmological principle.<br /> <br /> Still, there's always the Abyssal Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, one day I want to turn the Pyromancy and Miracle spells into martial arts each because chucking massive lightning spears is absolutely something a Solar should be able to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly just picture that as what Fiery Solar Chakram looks like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gael's mission to create a new world with the painting could inspire a jaded pessimistic Solar or Infernal with a similar mission of just restarting everything through some unfathomably powerful artifact)</div> </div> </div> </div>Gael to me is deeply Abyssal.<br /> <br /> The Painted World that chooses rot over fire informs some of my imagery of a prophetic Infernal's outlook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}